"url":"https://api.github.com/users/nireekshak","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### Description\r\n\r\nHello,\r\n\r\nWhen executing the below code and using chex to fake a multi-device environment on CPU, the return of `jnp.concatenate` returns incorrect values (a length-12 vector of 4s instead of 1s). When this code is run on a TPU runtime (without the `chex.set_n_cpu_devices` call), `jnp.concatenate` returns the correct length-12 vector of 1s.\r\n\r\n```\r\nimport chex\r\nimport jax\r\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\r\nfrom jax.experimental import mesh_utils\r\n\r\nchex.set_n_cpu_devices(8)\r\n\r\ndevices = mesh_utils.create_device_mesh((4, 2))\r\nmesh = jax.sharding.Mesh(devices, axis_names=('data', 'model'))\r\n\r\narray_one = jnp.ones((2,))\r\narray_two = jnp.ones((10,))\r\n\r\n# Fully replicate the first array.\r\nsharded_arr_one = jax.device_put(array_one, jax.sharding.NamedSharding(mesh, jax.sharding.PartitionSpec(None,)))\r\n# Shard the second array.\r\nsharded_arr_two = jax.device_put(array_two, jax.sharding.NamedSharding(mesh, jax.sharding.PartitionSpec('model',)))\r\n\r\nprint('Array one: ', sharded_arr_one)\r\nprint('Array two: ', sharded_arr_two)\r\nconcatenated = jnp.concatenate([sharded_arr_one, sharded_arr_two])\r\n\r\nprint('Concatenated array via jnp.concatenate: ', concatenated)\r\n```\r\n\r\ncc @yashk2810 \r\n\r\n### What jax/jaxlib version are you using?\r\n\r\njax v0.4.21\r\n\r\n### Which accelerator(s) are you using?\r\n\r\nCPU and TPU\r\n\r\n### Additional system info?\r\n\r\nNumpy version 1.26.2 \r\n\r\n### NVIDIA GPU info\r\n\r\n_No response_","closed_at":null,"closed_by":null,"comments":1,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19106/comments","created_at":"2023-12-22T23:18:38Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19106/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/19106","id":2054571234,"i